{#- Metrics exporters for the hosts that aren't Salt minions, as Podman
   containers on monitoring. All three are stateless.

   pve: prometheus-pve-exporter, multi-target — Prometheus passes the PVE
     node as ?target= (pillar/prometheus.sls job `pve`). Authenticates with
     a read-only API token (user/token_name here, token_value from OpenBao).
     verify_ssl False: the nodes' API certs are self-signed (same as the
     blackbox probes). Image user 101, writes nothing.
   fritzbox: pdreker/fritz_exporter (TR-064 + web UI), one device, configured
     by env. The image runs as 65534 and listens on 0.0.0.0 already.
     name = the friendly_name label. The password is at most 32 characters (the
     exporter refuses longer ones).
   truenas: graphite_exporter — TrueNAS SCALE pushes its Netdata reporting
     data as Graphite plaintext to graphite_port (Reporting → Exporters);
     the mapping file (Supporterino/truenas-graphite-to-prometheus, pinned
     release + sha256) turns it into Prometheus series. Strict match: only
     mapped paths become series. Runs as nobody (65534) and reads the
     root-owned 0644 mapping through the "other" bits.

   enabled: pve and fritzbox only render when pillar sets it — and
   pillar/infra-exporters.sls only sets it once the secret resolves, so a
   missing secret leaves monitoring as it was. truenas needs no secret.
   host_port / graphite_port: published on monitoring; Prometheus and
   TrueNAS point there.
   podman: spec overrides per container (keys: formulas/podman README). #}
